IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ct-tfa`

-- Connecticut temporary family assistance -- worked cases from the seat of the applicant (the parent or caretaker relative).
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against the
-- Uniform Policy Manual or a Department notice. Expected results were worked by hand from the deposited text.
-- The federal poverty level used is HYPOTHETICAL: $2,000 a month for the family's size (the real figure is published by HHS
-- each year and is not in commons). The regulative rules are asserted where the trace ends FULFILLED and #TRACEd, with an
-- "-- expect:" line, where it does not.

§ `Cases`

§§ `s 17b-75 -- dependent child`

#ASSERT `Is this child a dependent child` 17 FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- 18, full-time in high school, expected to finish before 19: still a dependent child.
#ASSERT `Is this child a dependent child` 18 TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- 18 and not in school: not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this child a dependent child` 18 FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- 18 in school but not expected to finish before 19: not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this child a dependent child` 18 TRUE FALSE TRUE)
-- 10 but not living with a listed or approved relative in that relative's home: not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is this child a dependent child` 10 FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `s 17b-104 -- standards`

-- 55% of $2,000 = $1,100.
#ASSERT `What is the TFA standard of need for my family` 2000 EQUALS 1100
-- 73% of $1,100 = $803.
#ASSERT `What is the TFA payment standard for my family` 2000 EQUALS 803

§§ `The amount, on this encoding's reading`

-- No income: the payment standard, $803.
#ASSERT `Roughly how much TFA would my family get` 2000 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 803
-- Subsidized housing: 8% of 803 = 64.24 attributed: $738.76.
#ASSERT `Roughly how much TFA would my family get` 2000 0 0 FALSE 0 TRUE EQUALS 738.76
-- Earnings $1,500, under the poverty level: "disregarded up to the federal poverty level", so still $803.
#ASSERT `Roughly how much TFA would my family get` 2000 1500 0 FALSE 0 FALSE EQUALS 803
-- Unearned income $300 counted: 803 - 300 = $503.
#ASSERT `Roughly how much TFA would my family get` 2000 0 0 FALSE 300 FALSE EQUALS 503
-- A (d)(2) month, earnings $3,000 (150%): disregarded up to 230%, below 171%, no reduction: $803.
#ASSERT `Roughly how much TFA would my family get` 2000 3000 0 TRUE 0 FALSE EQUALS 803
-- A (d)(2) month, earnings $3,600 (180%): disregarded, but between 171% and 230%: 80% of 803 = $642.40.
#ASSERT `Roughly how much TFA would my family get` 2000 3600 0 TRUE 0 FALSE EQUALS 642.4
-- Exactly 171% ($3,420): the reduction applies ("between" read inclusively).
#ASSERT `Roughly how much TFA would my family get` 2000 3420 0 TRUE 0 FALSE EQUALS 642.4

§§ `s 17b-112 -- eligibility`

-- A dependent child; earnings $1,500; assets $2,000; 10 months used; cooperates: eligible.
#ASSERT `Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 1500 0 FALSE 2000 10 FALSE 0 10 FALSE TRUE
-- No dependent child (and no other covered family): not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my family eligible for TFA` FALSE 2000 1500 0 FALSE 2000 10 FALSE 0 10 FALSE TRUE)
-- Earnings $2,500, over the poverty level, not a (d)(2) month: not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 2500 0 FALSE 2000 10 FALSE 0 10 FALSE TRUE)
-- The same $2,500, of which $600 is a student child's: $1,900 counted (s 17b-80(b)): eligible.
#ASSERT `Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 2500 600 FALSE 2000 10 FALSE 0 10 FALSE TRUE
-- Earnings $4,600 in a (d)(2) month: exactly 230%, "not to exceed": eligible. $4,601: not.
#ASSERT `Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 4600 0 TRUE 2000 10 FALSE 0 10 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 4601 0 TRUE 2000 10 FALSE 0 10 FALSE TRUE)
-- Assets of $6,000: not denied ("unless such assets exceed six thousand dollars"). $6,001: denied.
#ASSERT `Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 0 0 FALSE 6000 10 FALSE 0 10 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 0 0 FALSE 6001 10 FALSE 0 10 FALSE TRUE)
-- 36 months used, no exemption, no extension: past the limit.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 0 0 FALSE 0 36 FALSE 0 36 FALSE TRUE)
-- 36 months used, one six-month extension granted: within (36 < 42).
#ASSERT `Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 0 0 FALSE 0 36 FALSE 1 36 FALSE TRUE
-- 50 months used, exempt under (b): within the 36 months; but 60 months counted toward the 60-month limit: not.
#ASSERT `Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 0 0 FALSE 0 50 TRUE 0 50 FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 0 0 FALSE 0 60 TRUE 0 60 FALSE TRUE)
-- The same 60 months, with domestic violence: the 60-month limit does not apply.
#ASSERT `Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 0 0 FALSE 0 60 TRUE 0 60 TRUE TRUE
-- Not cooperating with child support enforcement: "ineligible for benefits".
#ASSERT NOT (`Is my family eligible for TFA` TRUE 2000 0 0 FALSE 0 10 FALSE 0 10 FALSE FALSE)

§§ `s 17b-112(c) -- extensions`

-- None granted yet, good faith, income $1,900 all earned: 1,900 - 90 = 1,810, below $2,000: shall grant.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner grant my extension` 0 TRUE 1900 1900 2000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner shall grant a six-month extension (s 17b-112(c))`
-- Income $2,050 all earned: the $90 disregard brings it to $1,960, below the poverty level: shall grant.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner grant my extension` 1 TRUE 2050 2050 2000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner shall grant a six-month extension (s 17b-112(c))`
-- Income $2,100 all earned: $2,010, not below: no duty, unless circumstances prevent employment.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner grant my extension` 0 TRUE 2100 2100 2000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 17b-112(c) does not require an extension on these facts`
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner grant my extension` 0 TRUE 2100 2100 2000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner shall grant a six-month extension (s 17b-112(c))`
-- Income $2,050 all unearned: no $90 earned disregard: not below: no duty.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner grant my extension` 0 TRUE 2050 0 2000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 17b-112(c) does not require an extension on these facts`
-- No good faith effort: no duty, even on low income.
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner grant my extension` 0 FALSE 500 500 2000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 17b-112(c) does not require an extension on these facts`
-- Two granted already: "not more than two"; a third only "may" be granted, where each adult meets (A), (B) or (C).
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner grant my extension` 2 TRUE 500 500 2000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner may grant a further six-month extension, because each adult meets a criterion in s 17b-112(c)(A) to (C)`
#ASSERT `Must the Commissioner grant my extension` 2 TRUE 500 500 2000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 17b-112(c) does not require an extension on these facts`

§§ `Deadlines`

-- Received 2 March 2026: 45 days later is 16 April 2026; with a disability determination, 60 days: 1 May 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must the Department act on my application` (Date 2 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS Date 16 4 2026
#ASSERT `By when must the Department act on my application` (Date 2 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS Date 1 5 2026
-- Not acted on: a hearing may be sought from 17 April 2026, not on 16 April.
#ASSERT `May I ask for a hearing because my application has not been acted on` (Date 2 3 2026) FALSE (Date 17 4 2026) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`May I ask for a hearing because my application has not been acted on` (Date 2 3 2026) FALSE (Date 16 4 2026) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`May I ask for a hearing because my application has not been acted on` (Date 2 3 2026) FALSE (Date 20 4 2026) TRUE)
-- New wages first received 1 May 2026: report by 11 May 2026.
#ASSERT `By when must I report it` (Date 1 5 2026) EQUALS Date 11 5 2026
#ASSERT `May I have a hearing on a TFA decision` TRUE
-- The Commissioner acts on day 30 of 45: fulfilled. With a disability determination, on day 55 of 60: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the Commissioner's duty to act on the application` FALSE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Commissioner of Social Services` `complete the investigation and act on the application` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the Commissioner's duty to act on the application` TRUE) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Commissioner of Social Services` `complete the investigation and act on the application` 55)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the Commissioner of Social Services, "application not acted on within the s 17b-80(a) period: ..." (acts on day 50 of 45)
#TRACE (`the Commissioner's duty to act on the application` FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner of Social Services` DOES `complete the investigation and act on the application` AT 50
-- Reported on day 10: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the duty to report income or a change` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the applicant or beneficiary` `notify the commissioner of the property, income or change` 10)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the applicant or beneficiary, "not reported within ten days (s 17b-85), unless the commissioner finds good cause" (day 12)
#TRACE `the duty to report income or a change` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the applicant or beneficiary` DOES `notify the commissioner of the property, income or change` AT 12
-- Reinvestigated in month 12: fulfilled.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE `the reinvestigation of my case` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Commissioner of Social Services` `reinvestigate the case` 12)) EQUALS FULFILLED
